Fixed the root cause in:

- `firmware/libopencm3-examples/examples/stm32/f4/stm32f4-discovery/button/button.c`

### Root cause
The code configures the user button on **PA0**:
```c
gpio_mode_setup(GPIOA, GPIO_MODE_INPUT, GPIO_PUPD_NONE, GPIO0);
```
but it was reading **PA1** in the blink-rate condition:
```c
if (gpio_get(GPIOA, GPIO1)) { ... }
```
So the button state was never actually sampled from the connected pin.

### Fix applied
Changed the readback pin from `GPIO1` to `GPIO0`:
```c
if (gpio_get(GPIOA, GPIO0)) {
```

This makes the slow-blink path activate correctly while the on-board button is held.
